This tender opportunity was issued by St Christopher's C of E (Primary) Multi Academy Trust (the Trust) and Contractors were invited to tender for the provision of ICT Managed Services (the Service). Full details of all contract requirements were given in Document 2. Specification of Requirement. The contract is intended to secure a high-quality, responsive and strategically aligned ICT managed service for the Trust. The Successful Contractor will be expected to deliver a service that: 
a. provides cost-effective, high-quality technical support, systems management and ICT consultancy;
b. offers transparent and comprehensive pricing to enable effective budget management across the contract term; c. acts as the Trust's single point of accountability for ICT support and for liaison with relevant third-party providers; d. and manages and supports the Trust's ICT environment across its full lifecycle, including strategic planning, implementation, maintenance, user support and continuous improvement.

Procurement for Housing (PfH) Scotland have established a dynamic purchasing system (DPS) for the delivery of capital works projects and provision of associated services for PfH Members throughout Scotland. It is intended that the DPS will run for an initial period of five year with an option to extend for a further period of up to five years. The opportunity has been divided into twelve categories as follows:
1) Whole House;
2) Kitchens;
3) Bathrooms;
4) Heating;
5) Electrical;
6) Windows and Doors;
7) Insulation;
8) Roofing;
9) Painting and Decorating;
10) Disabled Adaptations;
11) Skips / Waste Collection; and
12) Scaffolding.
Organisations can apply to become qualified suppliers in one or more lots. At the Invitation to Tender stage PfH Members will define the requirements including requirements and specification, delivery model and form of contract.

#Renewal of Specimen Transport consumables;
Tracked specimen delivery service; framework reference, RM6171, lot 3d
A specialised courier service operated by DX Network for the healthcare and clinical sectors in the UK and Ireland. It is specifically designed to handle the safe, compliant, and timely transportation of medical samples, such as Category B biological substances (including Covid-19 tests), from locations like hospitals, GPs, and laboratories.  The agreement is for the consumables related to the carriage of these samples.

The Authority has a Multi-Supplier Framework in place for the Provision of Removals, Relocations, Disposal and Storage Services which is due to expire on the 31st January 2027. The Authority is required to re-tender this opportunity. This will be the 3rd generation
Framework Agreement.
The Authority requires a Contractor(s) to deliver a variety of removal, relocation disposal and storage services for business and domestic properties, these services include the following points but not limited to:
- - Packing service of belongings (as and when requested by the Authority);
- - Dismantling and re-assembling items of furniture (as and when requested by the Authority);
- - Removal of business and domestic items, furniture and belongings from properties;
- - Storage of business and domestic items, furniture belongings from properties;
- - Delivery of business and domestic items, furniture belongings from properties;
- - Disposal of business and domestic items, furniture belongings from properties.

The procurement sought to appoint a suitably qualified and experienced roofing contractor to undertake roof renewal works at Byker Lodge, Bolam Way, Byker, Newcastle upon Tyne.
The works include:
•	removal of the existing roof coverings;
•	replacement boarding and insulation;
•	installation of a new single-ply roofing system;
•	replacement rooflights and access hatches;
•	associated rainwater goods and drainage connections;
•	perimeter trims and cladding;
•	scaffolding and site establishment;
•	waste removal;
